gcm/live-draw: diagnostics for surfaces of several sizes at one address and for antialiased targets (all off by default).

Written for Killzone 2's white half-screen (the causes were patches 2088 and 2089, not the two
colour surfaces at 0x7B0000 this was written to examine).
- LD_ALIAS_SIZE_LOG=N: texture binds and presents that resolve to a live surface of another size than declared, or
  whose texture or draw-target address holds two or more live surfaces (declared size, format and pitch, the draw's
  target, the surface picked and every candidate with its create/draw generations), and draw targets that are
  antialiased, wider than the window, or share their address (clip, aa grid, pitch, SURFACE_FORMAT, viewport,
  scissor and clip registers); one line per new combination, at most N lines each.
- LD_DRAW_INPUTS_VPW=<w>: with LD_DRAW_INPUTS (patch 2043) also select the draws whose viewport width is w (a pass
  whose index in the frame varies).
- The "[surfsz] new live surface" line names the frame.

Verification: Killzone 2 under Proton.
v0.17.0 rebase (ps3recomp a6d76c8): context only (#399 PS3_LOG_FIRST log caps and other upstream context); diff regenerated.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0: context and offsets only.

